{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>לִצְרֹר לְגַלּוֹת עֶרְוָתָהּ עָלֶיהָ בְּחַיֶּיהָ — to be a rival, to uncover her nakedness upon her during her lifetime.</b> Here Scripture explains the reason for the prohibition: it says that it is not fitting for a man to take a woman together with her sister, to make them rivals to one another, for they ought to be loving one another, not to be rivals (צָרוֹת). And Scripture did not say this in the case of a woman and her daughter (Leviticus 18:17) or a woman and her mother (Leviticus 20:14), because they are close kin (שְׁאֵר) and forbidden even after death."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:55:21.702952007Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}